#lead[Make no construction award under the current township rule. Request approval to fund unserved blocks and verify the addresses behind disputed claims. If the rule changes and providers sign leases, use county-owned backhaul for the first phase.]

*Why hold the grant.* Each of the six townships has at least one served flag, so none is eligible. North Ridge, West Plains and River Bend also fall short of the modeled 25% floor at baseline. North Ridge has up to 1,531 candidate households for a satellite-focused reclassification. Even a full correction there leaves four served blocks and does not unlock funding. Approve a separate evidence audit if legally and financially available. The base administrative allowance is \$12,585.

*What the amendment buys.* Under block eligibility, the county partnership adds #value("ppp_hh") qualifying household opportunities at #value("ppp_cost") over ten years. A sole cooperative award adds #value("coop_hh") for #value("coop_cost"). The partnership gains #value("advantage") more households while both clear the floor. The cooperative gives the county less direct exposure to asset renewal and tenant vacancy. If county evidence is also authorized to change eligibility and the North Ridge cases are verified, the partnership still leads at #value("override_count").

*Who gains and who pays.* Residents gain more orderable connections from the partnership, but their bills and installation needs still matter. The cooperative can bid for last-mile work and lease county capacity; it has no guaranteed award. A sole award gives it the entire allocation and responsibility for service. The national cable provider can bid or lease on the same terms as other providers under the partnership. It receives no construction grant under the sole award. Residential fees belong in the award review. Four hubs create a county maintenance obligation. Projected discounted rent of #value("ppp_rent") covers #value("om_recovery") of their discounted maintenance, leaving the county responsible for the remainder and the initial capital.

*Conditions before construction.* Obtain written permission for the revised eligibility rule. Verify orderability, alignments, wireless serviceability and capacity. Publish non-discriminatory lease terms and secure tenant commitments with a maintenance reserve. Test whether the household service can support work and school at the times people need it. If leases or field costs undermine the county plan and the revised rule is in force, use the cooperative as the fallback after confirming its countywide build capacity. #cite("1", "5", "16")

